Exactly. Your instinct to build a self-contained automation appliance was reasonable; **VCF 9 has moved a significant portion of the actual VCF deployment orchestration into the VCF Installer**. The Installer provides the deployment workflow, pre-checks, reusable JSON configuration, and deployment of the VCF stack. It does **not** carry the VCF binaries itself, so our air-gapped software source remains an external prerequisite. ([VMware Blogs][1])

